feature: INIT

requirements:
  - id: INIT-1
    title: Project Scaffolding
    description: >
      Running spool init in a project directory must set the project
      up for Spool: a .spool.yaml, a .spool/ directory with an example
      requirement, and a SPOOL.md guide.
    status: draft
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-10-30
    rationale: >
      Scaffolding previously lived only in the VS Code extension, in
      untested TypeScript that CLI users could not reach. Moving it
      into the binary makes it available everywhere, testable, and
      traced by Spool itself; editor extensions become thin wrappers
      that call it. Init never overwrites an existing file, because
      a project may already have requirements or its own SPOOL.md
      before it has a .spool.yaml.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: INIT-1-1
        title: Fresh Init
        description: >
          Given a directory with no .spool.yaml, .spool/ directory,
          or SPOOL.md,
          when spool init is run in it,
          then .spool.yaml, .spool/example.req, and SPOOL.md are
          created, each created path is printed, and it exits zero.

      - id: INIT-1-2
        title: Already Initialized
        description: >
          Given a directory that already has a .spool.yaml,
          when spool init is run in it,
          then it reports that the project is already initialized,
          changes nothing, and exits non-zero.

      - id: INIT-1-3
        title: Existing Files Preserved
        description: >
          Given a directory with no .spool.yaml but an existing
          SPOOL.md or .spool/ directory containing .req files,
          when spool init is run in it,
          then .spool.yaml is created, existing files are left
          unchanged, no example.req is added beside existing .req
          files, each skipped path is printed, and it exits zero.

      - id: INIT-1-4
        title: Generated Config Loads
        description: >
          Given a .spool.yaml written by spool init,
          when config is loaded,
          then no error is produced and its test_patterns and
          exclude_patterns equal what init detected.

      - id: INIT-1-5
        title: Generated Example Parses
        description: >
          Given a .spool/example.req written by spool init,
          when the reqs directory is parsed,
          then it parses without error.

  - id: INIT-2
    title: Project Type Detection
    description: >
      spool init must detect each kind of project present in the
      directory and write test_patterns and exclude_patterns
      suited to all of them.
    status: draft
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-10-30
    rationale: >
      Build output and dependency directories differ by language,
      and a project may mix languages. Detecting every project type
      from its manifest file and combining their patterns gives a
      working config on the first run, written out in full so the
      user can see and edit everything Spool will skip. Detection
      looks at any depth to find monorepo members, but never inside
      dependency or build directories, where manifests belong to
      third-party code.
    superseded_by:
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: INIT-2-1
        title: Go Project
        description: >
          Given a directory containing go.mod,
          when spool init is run,
          then test_patterns includes **/*_test.go and
          exclude_patterns includes **/vendor.

      - id: INIT-2-2
        title: Rust Project
        description: >
          Given a directory containing Cargo.toml,
          when spool init is run,
          then test_patterns includes **/*.rs and
          exclude_patterns includes **/target.

      - id: INIT-2-3
        title: JavaScript Project
        description: >
          Given a directory containing package.json,
          when spool init is run,
          then test_patterns includes **/*.{test,spec}.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}
          and exclude_patterns includes **/node_modules and **/dist.

      - id: INIT-2-4
        title: Java Project
        description: >
          Given a directory containing pom.xml, build.gradle,
          or build.gradle.kts,
          when spool init is run,
          then test_patterns includes **/src/test/**/*.java and
          exclude_patterns includes **/target and **/build.

      - id: INIT-2-5
        title: Mixed Project
        description: >
          Given a directory containing manifests for more than one
          project type,
          when spool init is run,
          then test_patterns and exclude_patterns contain the
          patterns of every detected type, each pattern once,
          in a stable order.

      - id: INIT-2-6
        title: Nested Manifest Detected
        description: >
          Given a manifest only in a subdirectory, such as
          crates/core/Cargo.toml,
          when spool init is run,
          then that project type is detected.

      - id: INIT-2-7
        title: Dependency Manifests Ignored
        description: >
          Given a manifest only inside a node_modules, vendor,
          target, dist, build, or .git directory,
          when spool init is run,
          then that project type is not detected.

      - id: INIT-2-8
        title: Unknown Project
        description: >
          Given a directory with no recognized manifest,
          when spool init is run,
          then .spool.yaml is written with empty test_patterns,
          a message says no project type was detected and that
          test_patterns must be edited, and it exits zero.
